+/*
+ * The same contract as the D3D11 presenter, on SDL2: producers copy a
+ * completed frame into a one-deep mailbox (pixel conversion included),
+ * the presenter thread owns the window, uploads the newest frame to a
+ * streaming texture and scales it with fb_present_rect(), and SDL events
+ * feed the same pc_input host-event functions Win32 messages feed on
+ * Windows (set-1 scancodes, relative mouse motion, wheel deltas of 120).
+ * Kelvin GPU shared-texture frames stay Windows-only: GpuWanted is 0, so
+ * the renderer keeps the CPU publication path, exactly as when the GPU
+ * backend is off there.
